==Portuguese==
{{wikipedia|lang=pt}}
[[file:Bahia in Brazil.svg|thumb|Bahia]]

===Alternative forms===
* {{alt|pt|Baía|Portugal}}

===Etymology===
Shortened from {{m|pt|Bahia de Todos os Santos||Bay of All Saints}}, after a bay on its coast.

{{m|pt|bahia}} is an archaic spelling of {{m|pt|baía||bay}}; the name of the state was specially mentioned as an exception in the Brazilian Orthographic Form of 1943, which otherwise removed {{angbr|h}} within words. However, derived terms such as {{m|pt|baiano}} (previously {{m|pt|bahiano}}) did not receive this treatment.

Although the {{w|Portuguese-Language Orthographic Agreement of 1990|Orthographic Agreement of 1990}} does not present any exceptions, this spelling is still officially adopted and listed in the {{w|Brazilian Academy of Letters}}’ Orthographic Vocabulary (''VOLP''). {{cln|pt|toponyms inconsistent with AO1990}}

